# Cursor Rules — Berkah POS SaaS

- Before any code, schema, deployment, CI, or architecture-document change, read root `AGENTS.md` and follow its mandatory reading order.
- `docs/permanent/DOC_00_CANONICAL_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` owns only the canonical five-layer configuration behavior and 352-entry workbook contract.
- `docs/permanent/ADR-2026-10-16-OWNER-ARCHITECTURE-DECISION.md` was accepted and merged by PR #49; it is the binding target decision for Laravel Central API on KVM2/Coolify with PostgreSQL 17, a central database and one database/restricted runtime role per tenant. This does not prove target implementation: at main baseline `d7ee23cfaada3405416b01d9e127e32b07fb1a38`, Flutter still uses `supabase_flutter` and the root has no Composer manifest/lockfile. `DOC_14_KVM2_ISOLATED_TENANT_ARCHITECTURE.md` details the gates and may not override the ADR.
- `docs/permanent/DOC_00_MASTER_ROADMAP.md` governs ordered phases; `DOC_12` and `DOC_13` contain supersession notices and must not be followed as authority for a new Supabase runtime.
- Canonical inheritance is `GLOBAL -> TEMPLATE -> TENANT -> SERVICE -> DEVICE`; exact workbook inventory is 352 entries (1 global + 3 templates + 100 tenants + 140 service entries + 108 devices).
- Separate these states in all claims: main implementation, accepted ADR target, implementation on open branches/PRs, exact-head CI results, staging observations and production deployment/acceptance. Retain Supabase source/data and historical reports as current-main implementation or migration evidence until verified, owner-approved cutover; never rewrite old reports to manufacture a pass. See `docs/reports/SOURCE_OF_TRUTH_ALIGNMENT_CORRECTION_2026-10-16.md`.
- Resolve one requested service at a time; never merge POS and Akuntansi rows.
- Keep the workbook as the source/export contract. The target Laravel importer maps its entries to normalized central tables; do not restore a generic Supabase `app_config(key, value JSONB)` runtime or the legacy `(device_id, key, value)` shape.
- Flutter runtime configuration and sync target the authenticated Laravel Central API, while SQLite local-first checkout/outbox remains mandatory.
- The shared application image serves standard tenants. Each tenant gets a distinct PostgreSQL database and restricted runtime role on one private PostgreSQL 17 service; a reviewed broker provisions these resources. Never use root/global DB credentials in tenant request handling.
- Admin/Central routes and tenant routes must be domain-scoped and independently authorized; a client-supplied tenant ID or Host header is not proof of access.
- Preserve offline idempotency, FEFO physical allocation vs FIFO financial costing, and accurate evidence reporting.
- Use branches and pull requests, never direct implementation pushes to `main`. Never force-push, erase `.git`, or delete existing files blindly.
- New workflows use GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-24.04`; deploy immutable images only after required checks pass.
- `scripts/sync_excel_to_supabase.py` is legacy workbook-sync code and contains a Supabase REST/RPC write path when cloud credentials are supplied. Do not execute it against an unknown/shared project as a validation step; require explicit source approval, backup and rollback. Its legacy name is not authorization to write to Supabase.
- Report unexecuted tests as `NOT RUN / NOT VERIFIED`; source presence and docs do not prove green CI, tenant isolation, successful restore, or production readiness.
